cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it. The current work is the
  key-resolution cost study in psao-artifact/paper/discarded-exception.tex.
  Earlier manuscripts in that directory are superseded and carry SUPERSEDED
  headers; material under results/, load-tests/ and the root manifests belongs
  to an earlier study and is retained for provenance.
title: "Replication package: where the cost of JWT verification actually goes"
abstract: >-
  Measurement, control and analysis code for a study of JSON Web Token
  verification cost in Kubernetes microservices under Istio. The dominant
  per-request cost is neither the signature primitive nor the conversion of key
  material, but a discarded exception: the library attempts an asymmetric key
  parse before the symmetric one and throws the failure away on every call. Its
  magnitude is governed by the bundled OpenSSL version rather than by the
  JavaScript engine or by containerisation. Includes the measurement harness
  (one condition per process), a four-runtime matrix, in-situ measurement across
  seven arrival rates, a prevalence survey with a hash-pinned corpus manifest,
  and the analysis pipeline that generates every numeric value in the paper.
type: software
